AirPods Seamless Switching for Ubuntu — credits and acknowledgements
=====================================================================

Upstream application
--------------------

This repository is a modified fork of EarPort by Anoryth and its contributors:
https://github.com/Anoryth/earport
License: GPL-3.0-or-later

Fork modifications for Max 2 support and audio handoff were made in August
2026.

The GNOME extension, daemon architecture, existing AirPods feature support,
and much of the source history come from that project. Git history and
copyright notices are retained.

Protocol research
-----------------

Apple Accessory Protocol parsing and the independently implemented handoff
messages are informed by the GPL-licensed LibrePods code and documentation:
https://github.com/librepods-org/librepods

The inherited EarPort protocol credits acknowledge LibrePods by Kavish Devar
(@kavishdevar), the wider LibrePods contributor community, and these protocol
and implementation contributors:

- @tyalie — protocol documentation
- @tim-gromeyer — Linux implementation work
- @devnoname120 — root patch assistance
- @rithvikvibhu — hearing-aid feature support

AirPods Max 2 classification and capability behavior were also cross-checked
against the MIT-licensed omarchy-pods project:
https://github.com/thisisgm/omarchy-pods

AirPods 4 and Max 2 BLE identifiers, public advertisement layout, and wear
bits were cross-checked against the GPL-licensed CAPod project:
https://github.com/d4rken-org/capod

The public AAP packet examples in tyalie/AAP-Protocol-Defintion include the
explicit current-wear-state request used by the polling fallback:
https://github.com/tyalie/AAP-Protocol-Defintion

That protocol-definition repository has no license file. Protocol bytes and
facts were referenced; no source code was incorporated from it.

The independent xatuke/handoff experiment helped demonstrate the intended
Apple/Linux ownership behavior:
https://github.com/xatuke/handoff

No source code was copied from xatuke/handoff; its repository does not include
a license file at the time this fork was prepared.

